    {
      "id": "dms_assume_role_scoped",
      "kind": "any_of",
      "checks": [
        {
          "kind": "attr",
          "select": "dmsvpc",
          "cond": {
            "path": "Policies.*.PolicyDocument.Statement.*",
            "op": "match",
            "value": [
              {
                "path": "Action.*",
                "op": "glob_covers",
                "value": "sts:AssumeRole"
              },
              {
                "path": "Resource.*",
                "op": "regex",
                "value": "arn:aws:iam::[^*]"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "attr",
          "select": "dmsvpc",
          "cond": {
            "path": "AssumeRolePolicyDocument.Statement.*",
            "op": "match",
            "value": [
              {
                "path": "Condition",
                "op": "regex",
                "value": "(?i)aws:(sourceaccount|principalaccount|resourceaccount|sourceowner|sourcearn|principalarn)"
              },
              {
                "path": "Condition",
                "op": "regex",
                "value": "([0-9]{12}|<param:)"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "attr",
          "select": "dmsvpc",
          "cond": {
            "path": "AssumeRolePolicyDocument.Statement.*.Principal.AWS.*",
            "op": "regex",
            "value": "^(arn:aws:iam::[^*]|[0-9]{12}$|<param:)"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "ref",
          "from": "assume_pol",
          "to": "dmsvpc",
          "bidirectional": true
        }
      ],
      "tier": "core",
      "quote": "The DMS VPC role must restrict its 'AssumeRole' policy statement using the provided Target Account ID parameter",
      "justify": "the AssumeRole statement can be the role policy or the trust policy, and either way it names an account rather than any account"
    },
    {
      "id": "kms_permissions",
      "kind": "any_of",
      "tier": "core",
      "quote": "any roles requiring KMS encryption or decryption permissions (such as the Firehose access role, the processing controller function role, and the worker role) must grant access",
      "justify": "the prompt names three roles that need the key; a statement limited to the key is not on Resource *",
      "checks": [
        {
          "kind": "exists",
          "min": 3,
          "select": {
            "types": [
              "AWS::IAM::Role"
            ],
            "where": [
              {
                "path": "Policies.*.PolicyDocument.Statement.*",
                "op": "match",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "path": "Action.*",
                    "op": "regex",
                    "value": "(?i)^kms:"
                  },
                  {
                    "path": "Resource.*",
                    "op": "none_eq",
                    "value": "*"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "ref",
          "from": "kms_pol",
          "to": "roles",
          "bidirectional": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tagged_roles",
      "kind": "exists",
      "select": "tagged",
      "tier": "detail",
      "quote": "ensure all roles are tagged with Project: DataMaster and Component: Roles",
      "justify": "nine service roles are listed and all must be tagged",
      "min": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "exported_arns",
      "kind": "exists",
      "select": "exports",
      "tier": "core",
      "quote": "export their ARNs utilizing a naming convention consisting of a 'dm-' prefix and a '-role-arn' suffix",
      "justify": "one export per role, nine service roles",
      "min": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "exports_are_arns",
      "kind": "attr",
      "select": "exports",
      "cond": {
        "path": "value",
        "op": "regex",
        "value": "(?i)(\"attr\": \"arn\"|^arn:)"
      },
      "tier": "detail",
      "quote": "export their ARNs",
      "quantifier": "all"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_dms_vpc_managed",
      "kind": "attr",
      "select": "dms",
      "cond": {
        "path": "ManagedPolicyArns",
        "op": "regex",
        "value": "AmazonDMSVPCManagementRole"
      },
      "tier": "extra"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_glue_managed",
      "kind": "attr",
      "select": "glue",
      "cond": {
        "path": "ManagedPolicyArns",
        "op": "regex",
        "value": "AWSGlueServiceRole"
      },
      "tier": "extra"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_ecs_managed",
      "kind": "attr",
      "select": "ecs",
      "cond": {
        "path": "ManagedPolicyArns",
        "op": "regex",
        "value": "AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy"
      },
      "tier": "extra"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_sfn_runtask",
      "kind": "attr",
      "select": "sfn",
      "cond": {
        "path": "Policies",
        "op": "regex",
        "value": "ecs:RunTask"
      },
      "tier": "extra"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt requires a KMS-key-ARN parameter and 'Do not create a KMS key', but the ground truth has no such parameter and creates an AWS::KMS::Key (roles reference it); prompt says ALL roles are tagged, but the ground truth leaves several lambda roles untagged and has only 10 tagged roles. So: no KMS parameter / no-KMS-key check, KMS grants checked as at least 3 roles with kms: statements on a specific key rather than *, tag check requires >=9 tagged roles. The generated extra check for AWS::KMS::Key was deleted because it would reward what the prompt forbids. Service roles are identified by trust-policy service principal, not names. kms_permissions also accepts a separate IAM policy with a key-scoped kms: statement attached to a role (a single policy can serve all three roles). The account-ID checks cannot compare a value with the parameter, so a hardcoded account passes dms_assume_role_scoped. DMS VPC role is identified by a name, description or policy naming DMS and VPC, or a dms.amazonaws.com trust plus ec2 network-interface permissions. Scored on 5 real candidates: DSV4F has no role granting DMS a Kinesis put action, Gemini38F has no DMS VPC role and prefixes its exports with the stack name (not 'dm-'); those failures are template defects and the checks stay."
}
